---
/**
 * CAREER DEVELOPMENT & STUDENT SUCCESS · SUBJECT SELECTION GUIDANCE — audit §2E.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS PAGE'S DEEP-DIVE IS THE EVIDENCE THAT THE CHOICE IS SUPPORTED, not a
 * description of how to choose a stream. Anyone can write "we help students
 * choose wisely". What this school can actually show is: the audience is named
 * on its own banner (Classes X and XI), the guidance is one-to-one at a desk,
 * and the outcome of the choice is published by name on a placement board.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — verified in this repository and on the school's own artwork ═══
 *   The four streams: PCM, PCB, Commerce, Humanities (data/site.ts school.streams).
 *   Career counselling is run for CLASS X & XI — read off the school's own
 *     hand-painted banner in its published photographs. Class X is the year
 *     before the choice; Class XI is the year it takes effect.
 *   The on-campus career counselling desk covers "subject choice, stream
 *     selection and university guidance" (data/facilities.ts).
 *   CUET (UG) 2025 results published for all three of PCM, Commerce and
 *     Humanities — the choice is followed all the way to the entrance paper.
 *   Guiding Futures, Shaping Lives — Classes IX–XII.
 *
 * ⚠ ELECTIVE LISTS ARE NOT REPEATED HERE. data/academics.ts warns that the
 * subject lists and the Humanities core are not verified; Subject Combinations
 * is the page that carries them, with its confidence labels attached. This page
 * names the four streams and sends the reader there rather than restating an
 * unverified list in a second place.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT CLAIMED: an aptitude test, a psychometric instrument, a deadline, or a
 * procedure for changing stream. None is published.
 *
 * Composition: path (paper, the four routes) → split (ivory, photo LEFT, the
 * desk where the choice is actually discussed) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcPath from '../../../components/academics/system/AcPath.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';
import { school as sb } from '../../../data/site';

import banner from '../../../assets/bio lab/DSC_1274 copy.jpg';
import pDesk from '../../../assets/school-activities/career-counselling/03.jpg';
import pChem from '../../../assets/chem lab/DSC_1262 copy.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-5.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';

/* The stream names only — never the elective lists, which live on Subject
   Combinations with their confidence labels. */
const streams = [...sb.streams];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Subject Selection Guidance — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="How the stream choice is supported at Sunbeam School Ballia: one-to-one counselling for Classes X and XI, four streams to board level, and CUET results published across all three streams."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Subject Selection Guidance"
    standfirst="The school's own banner says who this is for — Class X and Class XI. One year before the choice, and the year it lands."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Student Success', href: '/academics/student-success/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="A subject laboratory at Sunbeam School Ballia, benches and apparatus laid out along the room."
    position="50% 52%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcPath
      ground="paper"
      kicker="Four routes"
      heading="One choice,<br /><em>made once</em>"
      body={[
        'Sunbeam Ballia teaches four streams to CBSE board level. Choosing between them is the only decision on a student’s timetable that cannot easily be undone, which is why the guidance sits in Class X rather than in Class XI.',
        'What each stream contains — and how far each of those lists can be relied on — is set out on <strong>Subject Combinations</strong>, where the verified and the unverified are labelled as such. They are deliberately not restated here.',
      ]}
      beats={streams.map((s) => ({ k: s }))}
    />

    <AcSplit
      ground="ivory"
      side="left"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="Where it is actually discussed"
      heading="A desk, a laptop<br /><em>and one student</em>"
      body={[
        'The school’s stream guidance is not an assembly. Its published photographs show single students at a table with a counsellor working from a laptop, papers between them, and in several frames a parent or elder sibling in the next chair. The banner behind reads <strong>“Career Counseling — Class X &amp; XI.”</strong>',
        'That the guidance works through to the end is checkable rather than asserted: the school published <strong>CUET (UG) 2025 results in all three of PCM, Commerce and Humanities</strong>, and a placement board naming where those students went. A stream chosen in Class X is followed as far as the entrance paper it leads to.',
      ]}
      photo={pDesk}
      alt={`A student of ${school} and a family member in a one-to-one career counselling session, the school’s Class X and XI banner behind them`}
      inset={pChem}
      insetAlt={`The chemistry laboratory at ${school}, reagent shelves above the benches`}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Class X,<br /><em>not Class XI.</em>"
      body="The school publishes the four streams, the year groups its counselling is for, and the results that follow the choice. It does not publish an aptitude test, a deadline, or a procedure for changing stream — the office holds those."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Student council office-bearers and NCC cadets of ${school} on stage with the school’s dignitaries`}
      position="50% 38%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
